      "instructionSections": {},
      "instructions": "Ask Setup mode first, defaulting to Basic. Basic asks whether to create the Wiki and asks the user to confirm detected technology candidates; it persists Yes as wiki and No as none, displays Concurrent tasking No, Persistence none, Commit direct-main, installed core skill delivery, and technology skill delivery by-reference as Set values, and never displays Concurrent capacity. Advanced defaults concurrent tasking to No, asks capacity with default 3 only after Yes, defaults Persistence to file, Commit to direct-main, Documentation to both from wiki, specifications, or both, and technology delivery to by-reference. Read core skill delivery from consistent installed-agent and generation metadata, persist it without asking again, and block with exact regeneration and installation remediation when evidence is missing, invalid, inconsistent, byte-mismatched, or runtime-incompatible. A different project core mode requires explicit project-scoped native-agent regeneration and installation before PROJECT.yaml changes. Inspect representative project scopes, run setup-time technology detection once, compare every candidate and its evidence and conflicts with the technology skills exposed by the target runtime, and persist every candidate scope and skill disposition, the ordered accepted skill list, each rejection and reason, and a durable explicit user-confirmation reference; an empty or boolean-only confirmation is invalid. Create only the selected empty roots and required placeholders; none creates no documentation root. Never run reverse engineering or independent review during setup, and add documentation_mode only when a later explicit documentation workflow needs it. Record canonical workflow_selection.persistence and workflow_selection.commit independently, reconcile them with project_setup, migrate legacy provider and completion fields without changing intent, and keep provider-specific skills behind the Persistence router rather than adding them to Dev Coder. Select resource_coordination independently as none or agent-claim without folder overrides or a compatibility default. When agent-claim is selected, persist exactly the backlog-mutation, main-integration, browser-server, database-port, and live-model-evaluation deadline classes with maximum_duration_seconds and cleanup_grace_seconds, preserve exact resource-id overrides, verify exactly one deadline-capable agent-claim-helper-mcp or agent-claim-helper-command Provider Skill against agent-claim-helper, and render only that selected provider. Treat live external MCP parity as unavailable and unverified until claim_extend_deadline, claim_reset, and every interface input and result field are proven. When none is selected, omit coordination references, procedures, policy, helper interface, helper provider, worktree requirements, and evidence. Preserve ordered project-level skill extensions, valid maintainer edits, unsupported Azure DevOps and Jira placeholders, explicit UNSET boundaries, NO_VARIANT fallbacks, and detected required-but-unavailable BLOCKED outcomes. Conceptual agents own only technology-agnostic core skills and never list the selected resource-coordination implementation; repositoryMutation remains independent. Generate deterministic by-reference root or nested AGENTS.md folder guidance unless Advanced explicitly selects inline technology delivery, plus thin Claude bridges. Validate every referenced definition, skill, route, runtime capability, and bridge. Never infer project-owned selectors from files, remotes, hosting metadata, templates, plugins, or available tools, and do not copy a selected resource-coordination procedure into project guidance.",
      "modelProfile": "default",
      "modelStages": {},
      "name": "project-configurator",
      "outputPurposes": {
        "AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md routing": "Connects the validated configuration to the operational files that supported runtimes actually load while working in each scope.",
        "PROJECT.yaml": "Gives reviewers and generators one inspectable source of truth for the project's conceptual agent definitions, skillsets, and routing decisions.",
        "nested AGENTS.md recommendations": "Identifies where folder-specific agent guidance is necessary so distinct technical or organizational boundaries are not flattened into the root configuration.",
        "runtime capability validation": "Confirms that selected conceptual agent definitions declare repository mutation independently and that the target runtime can load the selected resource-coordination policy skill plus one verified agent-claim-helper Provider Skill when applicable.",
        "setup selections": "Records Basic or Advanced mode, Set values, documentation roots, installed core delivery, confirmed technologies, and technology delivery.",
        "technology detection skillsets": "Records the evidence-backed technology skills, missing requirements, conflicts, and no-variant outcomes that folder guidance must preserve.",
        "validation evidence": "Gives reviewers confidence that conceptual agent definitions, skills, paths, and generated guidance were checked against both project evidence and bundle requirements.",
        "workflow selectors": "Records independent Persistence and Commit identifiers and deterministic legacy migration while generated guidance names only selected workflow skills."
      },
      "outputs": [
        "PROJECT.yaml",
        "technology detection skillsets",
        "nested AGENTS.md recommendations",
        "runtime capability validation",
        "setup selections",
        "workflow selectors",
        "AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md routing",
        "validation evidence"
      ],
